    "document": "tenancy_terms_evidence",
    "point": "op_a925ebc42ebd1e45369b1fd831c2e892",
    "text": "Cases / Synthetic claim / Recorded investigation\n\nRepeated heating failure and reported repair calls\n\nLive rules-based check · historical synthetic packet · as of 2025-02-21\n\nWorking. Earlier findings · new sources await review.\n\nSkip to result\nPause\nChoose case\nHistory\nProcess\nDocuments\nKnowledge\nSources\n\nDerive document requirement\n\n01-customer-and-tenancy-clarification.txt ↗\nSynthetic demonstration document (fictional)\nSource date: 2025-02-21\nReview as-of: 2025-02-21\n\nI, Riley Foster, am the tenant under an indefinite ordinary residential lease for Synthetic Rosenweg 33, 8008 Zurich, canton Zurich. The landlord is Synthetische Wohnraum AG. Current monthly net rent is CHF1800; the landlord maintains the fixed central heating and circulation pump. The lease requires usable heated living rooms in winter.\n\nMy active request is removal of the continuing heating defect and assessment of proportional rent-reduction eligibility from the landlord's first knowledge until remedy. I report no incurred monetary loss, no health-compensation claim, no self-help expense and no deposit/withholding request. The repair is not complete; no reduction percentage or award has been agreed.\n\n\nRelevant tenancy terms\n\nInspect operation\n\nWorking model · provisional Inspect calculation\n\nEstablish relevant tenancy terms\nOpen larger process\n·\nCapture the reported defect\n·\nEstablish relevant tenancy terms\nApplicability · Applies\nExecution · Waiting for Capture the reported defect\n·\nEstablish landlord knowledge\n·\nAssess supported cause\n·\nAssess objective defect evidence\n·\nRecord repair and rent reduction eligibility\n\nRequirement calculation · Relevant tenancy terms Inspect"
